Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.10,0:00:16.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, Yermis! He's there! Call a doctor!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.98,0:00:19.63,Default,,0,0,0,,He should have healed\Nfrom the snails by now!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.12,0:00:24.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Emporio! Jolene!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.14,0:00:26.18,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm sorry, the wind has stopped.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.26,0:00:28.82,Default,,0,0,0,,The rainbow disappeared, too. See, Jolene?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.98,0:00:35.32,Default,,0,0,0,,In his final few days, he was happy.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:36.68,0:00:38.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Weather had already been saved.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.00,0:00:41.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Weather.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:46.66,0:00:48.16,Default,,0,0,0,,One more time.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.50,0:00:51.40,Default,,0,0,0,,I want to speak with you.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:51.86,0:00:53.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Just one more time.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.12,0:00:56.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Just once more.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:57.56,0:00:59.97,Default,,0,0,0,,I want to talk to you in the soft breeze.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:29.18,0:01:30.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Weather forecast.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.08,0:01:33.50,Default,,0,0,0,,You never gave up.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:33.86,0:01:38.04,Default,,0,0,0,,In your final moments, you were trying\Nto tell me to pursue the priest.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:38.70,0:01:42.30,Default,,0,0,0,,You even took advantage of Palesnake's\Nability to upload your stand,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:42.38,0:01:43.40,Default,,0,0,0,,weather forecast,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:43.80,0:01:45.15,Default,,0,0,0,,onto a disc of its own.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:46.90,0:01:49.67,Default,,0,0,0,,If I were to stick this\Ndisc inside of my head,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:49.92,0:01:52.50,Default,,0,0,0,,would I be able to use your abilities too?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:54.14,0:01:56.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Although the priest has\Nalready started making
Dialogue: 0,0:01:56.64,0:02:00.40,Default,,0,0,0,,his way toward Cape\NCanaveral only two more days
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.48,0:02:04.48,Default,,0,0,0,,until the new moon at\Nthis point I don't know if
Dialogue: 0,0:02:04.56,0:02:07.50,Default,,0,0,0,,I can even take control\Nof this situation anymore.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:08.80,0:02:13.48,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm so lost what do I do despite the snail
Dialogue: 0,0:02:13.56,0:02:16.58,Default,,0,0,0,,apocalypse we just dealt\Nwith dad's disc was given
Dialogue: 0,0:02:16.66,0:02:20.40,Default,,0,0,0,,To the Speed Wagon\NFoundation, my old man will
Dialogue: 0,0:02:20.48,0:02:23.08,Default,,0,0,0,,regain consciousness\Nagain and he'll know what
Dialogue: 0,0:02:23.16,0:02:27.12,Default,,0,0,0,,needs to be done should\NI wait for him or not
Dialogue: 0,0:02:27.20,0:02:30.78,Default,,0,0,0,,but while I'm waiting\Nfor him the priest might
Dialogue: 0,0:02:30.86,0:02:33.42,Default,,0,0,0,,perpetrate an evil act\Nagain in cape canaveral
Dialogue: 0,0:02:33.50,0:02:38.08,Default,,0,0,0,,oh dad what should I
Dialogue: 0,0:02:38.16,0:02:41.64,Default,,0,0,0,,do please dad tell me?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:43.66,0:02:48.43,Default,,0,0,0,,If I had never gotten inside of that car,\NWeather might still be alive right now.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:48.96,0:02:52.86,Default,,0,0,0,,No, I must go to Cape Canaveral.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:53.24,0:02:55.40,Default,,0,0,0,,I have to take care of the priest.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:56.22,0:02:58.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Please, Dad, give me a sign.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:59.16,0:03:01.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Just what is it that I\Ncan do at this point?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:02.30,0:03:03.32,Default,,0,0,0,,What is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:21.88,0:03:26.94,Default,,0,0,0,,thread of lies
Dialogue: 0,0:03:29.76,0:03:36.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Itaami o noi Cairo tabi
Dialogue: 0,0:03:36.50,0:03:40.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Kokoro wa eilu
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.36,0:03:44.02,Default,,0,0,0,,ni togisuma
Dialogue: 0,0:03:44.10,0:03:49.58,Default,,0,0,0,,sareru Cairo kai sareru
Dialogue: 0,0:03:49.66,0:03:54.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Chaka mei no sai hate de
Dialogue: 0,0:04:50.74,0:04:51.57,Default,,0,0,0,,She's...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:51.65,0:04:52.72,Default,,0,0,0,,she's so cute.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:53.26,0:04:54.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, wow.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:55.72,0:04:57.46,Default,,0,0,0,,How is she so cute?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:58.54,0:05:01.78,Default,,0,0,0,,And she's even cuter sleeping\Non my shoulder like that.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:02.36,0:05:03.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Jolene.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:04.18,0:05:05.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, that's right.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:05.66,0:05:07.54,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm finally around Jolene again.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:07.84,0:05:10.94,Default,,0,0,0,,I made a promise to myself that\Nwhen I got out of prison and
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.02,0:05:14.14,Default,,0,0,0,,finally caught up to Jolene that\NI'd tell her how I feel about her.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:14.22,0:05:16.34,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't have any more time to waste.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:16.46,0:05:19.52,Default,,0,0,0,,If I don't tell her now, I\Nwon't get another chance.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:19.70,0:05:22.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Fact is, my feelings for her are genuine.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:22.72,0:05:23.55,Default,,0,0,0,,After all,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:23.63,0:05:27.03,Default,,0,0,0,,I paid a whole fortune to get my hands\Non this ring while I was in prison.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:27.12,0:05:29.00,Default,,0,0,0,,When she wakes from her slumber,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:29.58,0:05:31.20,Default,,0,0,0,,all I ask from her is?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:31.72,0:05:34.50,Default,,0,0,0,,to know and embrace how I truly feel.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:35.66,0:05:36.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Yo, check it!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:37.34,0:05:38.64,Default,,0,0,0,,You see those gators?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:38.96,0:05:41.46,Default,,0,0,0,,The alligators have come\Nall the way out here!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:41.54,0:05:42.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Damn it.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:42.76,0:05:46.00,Default,,0,0,0,,I think they're so goddamn safe\Nbecause they're federally protected?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:46.08,0:05:48.08,Default,,0,0,0,,but they scared the crap\Nout of us back in prison.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:48.16,0:05:48.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Hold on!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:49.07,0:05:49.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you serious?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:50.12,0:05:51.12,Default,,0,0,0,,That one's massive!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:51.20,0:05:53.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Eat this, asshole! Screw you!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:54.06,0:05:56.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Ha! Bullseye! Hell yeah!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.34,0:05:58.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Look at him freaking out.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:58.88,0:06:00.52,Default,,0,0,0,,I think you scared it, Jolene.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:00.60,0:06:02.44,Default,,0,0,0,,It ain't running, but it's flipping out.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:02.52,0:06:05.96,Default,,0,0,0,,That ought to teach you lizards not to\Nmess with us, you stupid, filthy animals.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:06.04,0:06:06.87,Default,,0,0,0,,No way.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:06.95,0:06:07.78,Default,,0,0,0,,She didn't.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:08.72,0:06:09.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Jolene!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:09.63,0:06:11.02,Default,,0,0,0,,What did you just throw?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:12.66,0:06:13.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Let me see.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:13.57,0:06:15.52,Default,,0,0,0,,Show me your hands right now!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:16.20,0:06:17.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Huh? Wait, what?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:18.08,0:06:18.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Yo, chill.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:19.10,0:06:20.12,Default,,0,0,0,,What's your deal, Anastasia?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:20.20,0:06:23.70,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm telling you to open up your hands\Nand show them to me immediately!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:23.78,0:06:24.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, what the hell?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:24.86,0:06:27.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Seriously, why are you\Ngetting so upset, Anastasia?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:27.40,0:06:29.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Did you really just throw it?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:29.58,0:06:31.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Please don't tell me you did!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:31.34,0:06:33.18,Default,,0,0,0,,You didn't just throw it away!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:44.34,0:06:46.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Urmas, can you do a favor for me?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:46.78,0:06:49.72,Default,,0,0,0,,I want to take a look at\Na map to study the area.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:50.20,0:06:52.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Can you hold on to this for a second?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:52.18,0:06:53.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Sure.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:56.82,0:06:58.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, that makes sense.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:58.58,0:07:00.60,Default,,0,0,0,,When you said map, you meant this.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:01.08,0:07:03.43,Default,,0,0,0,,This computer is a total fossil, though.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:06.94,0:07:09.12,Default,,0,0,0,,This is where we are, Cape Canaveral.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:09.52,0:07:11.05,Default,,0,0,0,,At coordinates 28 degrees,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:11.20,0:07:14.18,Default,,0,0,0,,24 minutes north, and 80\Ndegrees, 36 minutes west,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:14.36,0:07:17.24,Default,,0,0,0,,it's the section of Florida\Nthat juts out in the Atlantic.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:17.32,0:07:20.70,Default,,0,0,0,,It's located on a shoal\Nof 34,000 hectares.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:20.94,0:07:24.46,Default,,0,0,0,,where wildlife and ancient\Nnature still remain. A shoal?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:24.82,0:07:28.86,Default,,0,0,0,,It's a part of land which is an\Naccumulation of sediment from a river.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:28.94,0:07:31.88,Default,,0,0,0,,And this place is where\Nwe're currently headed to.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:32.38,0:07:33.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Space Center.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:34.00,0:07:36.46,Default,,0,0,0,,There are no trains or\Nbuses leading to it,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:36.54,0:07:38.72,Default,,0,0,0,,and you can only get\Nthere by driving a car.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:38.80,0:07:42.32,Default,,0,0,0,,With their devotion to space travel,\Nthey focus on launching rockets,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:42.40,0:07:45.00,Default,,0,0,0,,satellites, and space shuttles\Ninto the great unknown.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:45.08,0:07:47.86,Default,,0,0,0,,This structure right here is\Nthe Vehicle Assembly Building,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:47.94,0:07:50.74,Default,,0,0,0,,and that's the Launching\NComplex and Observation Gantry.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:50.82,0:07:54.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Being more than five kilometers\Napart shows how big this place is.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.78,0:07:57.30,Default,,0,0,0,,We'll be heading to the\NVisitor Center first.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:57.38,0:07:59.66,Default,,0,0,0,,All visitors who come\Nhere must enter this way
Dialogue: 0,0:07:59.74,0:08:01.88,Default,,0,0,0,,before they can explore\Nthe rest of the complex.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:01.96,0:08:03.94,Default,,0,0,0,,There, the visitors will purchase tickets,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:04.02,0:08:07.54,Default,,0,0,0,,go through security checks, and then\Nget on a shuttle bus for a tour.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:07.62,0:08:11.44,Default,,0,0,0,,For safety reasons, all other\Nareas are off-limits to the public.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:11.82,0:08:14.34,Default,,0,0,0,,It's most likely that\Nthe priest made his way
Dialogue: 0,0:08:14.42,0:08:16.36,Default,,0,0,0,,into the center by taking\Nthis route as well,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:16.44,0:08:19.44,Default,,0,0,0,,though I still have no idea\Nwhat his true agenda here is.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:19.52,0:08:21.66,Default,,0,0,0,,He's probably going to\Nlay low somewhere inside
Dialogue: 0,0:08:21.74,0:08:24.56,Default,,0,0,0,,the Space Center until\Nthe time of the new moon.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:25.94,0:08:27.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Okay, stop right there.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:28.34,0:08:32.04,Default,,0,0,0,,For security measures, we're limiting the\Nnumber of guests allowed in right now.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:32.12,0:08:33.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Please wait here for a moment.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:34.88,0:08:35.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Apologies, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:36.04,0:08:37.44,Default,,0,0,0,,That gentleman is with me.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:37.52,0:08:39.58,Default,,0,0,0,,One more guest won't hurt, will it?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:40.92,0:08:42.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on, get in here.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:47.44,0:08:51.50,Default,,0,0,0,,You would have had to wait another\N15 minutes before they let you in.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:52.08,0:08:55.40,Default,,0,0,0,,So tell me, you a pastor,\Nor could you be a priest?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:56.00,0:08:58.42,Default,,0,0,0,,I try to do one good deed a day.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:58.68,0:09:01.10,Default,,0,0,0,,It's sort of like a personal\Ngoal I've set for myself.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:01.18,0:09:02.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you sightseeing?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:02.34,0:09:03.42,Default,,0,0,0,,You know, it's just,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:03.50,0:09:06.92,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm curious why a man of God like you\Nis interested in all this space stuff.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:07.00,0:09:09.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Because if you ask me, you\Nlook a little out of place.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:09.82,0:09:12.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, actually, it kind\Nof makes sense, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:12.28,0:09:14.54,Default,,0,0,0,,God and space are sort\Nof similar, you know?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:14.62,0:09:17.44,Default,,0,0,0,,And who can say, maybe\NGod is actually an alien?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:17.64,0:09:19.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Uh, that's just a little joke.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:19.08,0:09:19.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Did I offend?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:21.28,0:09:25.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you expecting me to humor these\Nridiculous questions with an answer?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:25.30,0:09:26.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Eh?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:26.40,0:09:29.50,Default,,0,0,0,,You did your good deed for\Nthe day, isn't that enough?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:29.58,0:09:33.23,Default,,0,0,0,,If this is your idea of killing\Ntime, go do it somewhere else.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:33.34,0:09:35.00,Default,,0,0,0,,It's not like I was in such a hurry that I
Dialogue: 0,0:09:35.08,0:09:37.74,Default,,0,0,0,,could not have waited\Nanother measly 15 minutes,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:37.82,0:09:38.65,Default,,0,0,0,,you know.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:45.08,0:09:47.76,Default,,0,0,0,,The trickiest part of\Nlaunching a spacecraft into
Dialogue: 0,0:09:47.84,0:09:50.88,Default,,0,0,0,,outer space is the unpredictable\Nproblem of gravity.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:50.96,0:09:52.37,Default,,0,0,0,,When launching a rocket,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:52.50,0:09:56.72,Default,,0,0,0,,even the slightest variation in\Ngravitational pull can make a difference.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:56.80,0:09:59.04,Default,,0,0,0,,That is why when building a launch pad,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:59.12,0:10:02.66,Default,,0,0,0,,it is most effective to construct\Nit near the Earth's equator.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:02.74,0:10:05.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Because of the centrifugal\Nforce of the Earth's rotation,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:05.92,0:10:09.56,Default,,0,0,0,,the gravitational pull at the\Nequator is weaker than at the poles.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:09.64,0:10:12.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Perhaps Olympic highdivers\Nmight be able to
Dialogue: 0,0:10:12.28,0:10:15.34,Default,,0,0,0,,achieve a better record if\Nthey're near the equator.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:16.42,0:10:17.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Something's off.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:17.58,0:10:18.56,Default,,0,0,0,,I feel odd.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:18.86,0:10:23.70,Default,,0,0,0,,On top of that, here in Cape Canaveral,\Nthe sea level offshore is quite distinct.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:24.36,0:10:27.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Typically, sea level is marked\Nzero meters above sea level.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:28.30,0:10:29.13,Default,,0,0,0,,However,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:29.21,0:10:30.83,Default,,0,0,0,,scientific studies in recent years have
Dialogue: 0,0:10:30.92,0:10:33.56,Default,,0,0,0,,shown that sea levels\Noften vary by location.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:33.64,0:10:36.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's take the Maldives of\Nthe Indian Ocean, for example.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:37.08,0:10:41.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Research shows that sea level offshore\Nis close to 100 meters below sea level.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:42.26,0:10:46.42,Default,,0,0,0,,On the other hand, it's about 30 meters\Nabove sea level near the Sea of Japan.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:46.50,0:10:50.85,Default,,0,0,0,,And offshore here in Cape Canaveral,\Nit's about 50 meters above sea level.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:51.04,0:10:54.08,Default,,0,0,0,,In other words, gravity isn't\Nthe same everywhere on Earth.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:54.16,0:10:57.87,Default,,0,0,0,,And it can be said that gravity\Nis weak here in Cape Canaveral.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:58.32,0:10:59.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Also,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:59.23,0:11:00.85,Default,,0,0,0,,depending on the current\Nphase of the moon,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:00.94,0:11:04.36,Default,,0,0,0,,sea level can rise as high as\N100 meters above sea level.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:05.54,0:11:08.48,Default,,0,0,0,,It is for this reason the Cape\NCanaveral is one of the most
Dialogue: 0,0:11:08.56,0:11:11.85,Default,,0,0,0,,optimal locations on Earth\Nto launch rockets into space.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:19.60,0:11:20.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Huh? What was that?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:45.22,0:11:46.05,Default,,0,0,0,,What the?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:46.13,0:11:47.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Where's my drink?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:09.92,0:12:12.44,Default,,0,0,0,,So, Jolene, what are you planning to do?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:13.10,0:12:16.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Are we waiting for the Speedwagon\NFoundation and your dad to arrive?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:16.68,0:12:21.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Or would you rather drop that plan and\Nkeep pursuing the priest by ourselves?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:22.88,0:12:23.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Well.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:24.30,0:12:26.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Of course we're still\Ngoing after the priest.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:27.24,0:12:30.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Sorry to say this, but we don't even\Nknow if your father is going to make it.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:30.94,0:12:32.82,Default,,0,0,0,,That might be two days from now.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:33.42,0:12:37.16,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm sure the priest's wounds from his fight\Nwith weather haven't healed yet either.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:37.24,0:12:38.59,Default,,0,0,0,,And he's out of allies.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:38.80,0:12:39.92,Default,,0,0,0,,This is our chance.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:40.20,0:12:42.96,Default,,0,0,0,,The only thing we know for sure is\Nthat if we don't finish him now,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:43.04,0:12:45.33,Default,,0,0,0,,it's going to be the end for all of us.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:52.02,0:12:53.37,Default,,0,0,0,,What the hell, Emporia?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:53.50,0:12:54.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Why are you driving so weird?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:55.04,0:12:56.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Stop all that fidgeting.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:56.64,0:12:58.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't you know we can't park the car here?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:58.44,0:12:59.79,Default,,0,0,0,,No, it's not like that.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:01.20,0:13:03.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, I'm telling you to move the damn car.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:03.54,0:13:05.12,Default,,0,0,0,,You do realize we stole this ride?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:05.20,0:13:06.84,Default,,0,0,0,,And every last one of us is still wanted!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:06.92,0:13:08.44,Default,,0,0,0,,for breaking out of prison, remember?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:08.52,0:13:10.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Plus, we got a kid in the driver's seat.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:10.64,0:13:12.29,Default,,0,0,0,,No, you've got it all wrong.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:12.56,0:13:14.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Something's going on with the car.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:14.48,0:13:15.31,Default,,0,0,0,,What is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:15.40,0:13:17.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't know, but it's stalling now.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:32.50,0:13:34.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Hermes, you should drive instead.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:40.32,0:13:41.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:47.80,0:13:49.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Yo, what the hell?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:49.28,0:13:50.22,Default,,0,0,0,,What's going on?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:10.24,0:14:11.42,Default,,0,0,0,,No way!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:13.08,0:14:14.56,Default,,0,0,0,,It's gonna hit us!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:19.96,0:14:21.00,Default,,0,0,0,,The fuck?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:21.26,0:14:22.32,Default,,0,0,0,,The cars!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:22.58,0:14:24.64,Default,,0,0,0,,When does this crazy shit\Nkeep happening to us?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:24.72,0:14:25.55,Default,,0,0,0,,What blew up?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:25.63,0:14:27.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Was there an accident or something?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:27.56,0:14:29.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Emporio, get it in gear!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:29.66,0:14:30.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Start the car already!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:31.78,0:14:33.08,Default,,0,0,0,,I... I can't!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:33.82,0:14:35.30,Default,,0,0,0,,It isn't moving at all!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:35.52,0:14:37.24,Default,,0,0,0,,I think the road is collapsing!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:37.32,0:14:38.15,Default,,0,0,0,,You're wrong!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:38.23,0:14:39.06,Default,,0,0,0,,It's not the road!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:39.15,0:14:40.80,Default,,0,0,0,,There's nothing wrong with it!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:40.88,0:14:42.56,Default,,0,0,0,,The guardrail's still standing too!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:42.64,0:14:45.17,Default,,0,0,0,,And there's no wind\Nblowing it away either!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:48.90,0:14:52.50,Default,,0,0,0,,You might be wondering what the hell\NI'm doing right about now, Jolene.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:52.58,0:14:53.48,Default,,0,0,0,,But I...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:53.56,0:14:54.90,Default,,0,0,0,,I think I'm stuck!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:55.42,0:14:59.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Hanging on to this car, this\Nis bad. Jolene get out of
Dialogue: 0,0:15:00.00,0:15:02.72,Default,,0,0,0,,the car it's not safe in\Nthere we're all gonna have to
Dialogue: 0,0:15:02.80,0:15:06.66,Default,,0,0,0,,bail we don't hurry up and\Nmake a move we're gonna keep
Dialogue: 0,0:15:06.74,0:15:09.88,Default,,0,0,0,,falling we're not falling\Ndown we're falling backwards
Dialogue: 0,0:15:09.96,0:15:13.40,Default,,0,0,0,,did you say that we're\Nfalling all the other cars
Dialogue: 0,0:15:13.48,0:15:16.36,Default,,0,0,0,,went falling backwards behind\Nus it's almost like this
Dialogue: 0,0:15:16.44,0:15:19.20,Default,,0,0,0,,road is a cliff the car's\Nstarting to shake all over
Dialogue: 0,0:15:19.28,0:15:21.72,Default,,0,0,0,,the place the front tires are\Nalready lifting off of the
Dialogue: 0,0:15:21.80,0:15:24.52,Default,,0,0,0,,ground now move it like\Ni said and get out of the
Dialogue: 0,0:15:24.60,0:15:28.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Car, no, this can't be. Is\Nthis the priest's new ability?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:28.32,0:15:31.66,Default,,0,0,0,,it's not even the new moon\Nyet that's impossible the
Dialogue: 0,0:15:31.74,0:15:34.16,Default,,0,0,0,,force of the pole just keeps\Ngetting stronger and we're
Dialogue: 0,0:15:34.24,0:15:37.38,Default,,0,0,0,,starting to fall sideways\Nget out you guys hurry and
Dialogue: 0,0:15:37.46,0:15:43.42,Default,,0,0,0,,fail before the car flips over\Nwe're not falling downward
Dialogue: 0,0:15:43.50,0:15:46.38,Default,,0,0,0,,we're falling parallel to\Nthe ground but how far are
Dialogue: 0,0:15:46.46,0:15:52.78,Default,,0,0,0,,we going to fall Jolene here\Nyou grab a hold of Emporio
Dialogue: 0,0:15:56.64,0:15:57.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Diver, drive!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:10.56,0:16:11.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Hermes!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:12.88,0:16:14.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Stone Ocean!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:15.68,0:16:17.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Where did you go, Hermes?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:17.74,0:16:19.56,Default,,0,0,0,,How far are you going to fall?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:20.00,0:16:21.52,Default,,0,0,0,,We're starting to slide!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:21.60,0:16:25.00,Default,,0,0,0,,If we don't do something fast,\Nwe're gonna crash into the rubble!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:25.08,0:16:27.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Jolene, you gotta forget about Hermes!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:27.12,0:16:29.20,Default,,0,0,0,,If she's not dead, she'll catch up to us!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:29.28,0:16:30.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, but she...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:32.24,0:16:34.40,Default,,0,0,0,,The priest is still somewhere up ahead.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:34.48,0:16:38.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you saying we should go back instead\Nof pursuing him like we promised?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:38.30,0:16:40.12,Default,,0,0,0,,You've done everything you can!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:40.36,0:16:43.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Jolene, your body is going\Nto crack under the pressure!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:52.20,0:16:54.82,Default,,0,0,0,,This must be it, isn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:00.94,0:17:02.34,Default,,0,0,0,,You're falling sideways?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:02.42,0:17:05.56,Default,,0,0,0,,I just don't get how we can\Nfall parallel to the ground!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:05.64,0:17:08.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Is it gravity supposed to keep you\Nplanted on the Earth's surface?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:08.56,0:17:11.26,Default,,0,0,0,,This is exactly what the\Npriest was waiting for!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:11.34,0:17:15.04,Default,,0,0,0,,I knew my old man sealed away some\Nsort of ability in Egypt 20 years ago,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:15.12,0:17:16.24,Default,,0,0,0,,but this is insane!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:16.76,0:17:20.17,Default,,0,0,0,,This must be the heaven the\Npriest has been searching for!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:23.36,0:17:25.95,Default,,0,0,0,,There are some plants\Nthat aren't uprooting.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:26.10,0:17:30.16,Default,,0,0,0,,It looks like the Visitor Center\Nbuilding hasn't fully collapsed yet.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:30.30,0:17:31.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, wait a minute, Jolene.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:32.34,0:17:34.58,Default,,0,0,0,,You just called this heaven, didn't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:34.66,0:17:36.16,Default,,0,0,0,,But I don't think that's it.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:36.24,0:17:38.04,Default,,0,0,0,,This is just the beginning.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:39.04,0:17:43.52,Default,,0,0,0,,I've got a bad feeling that this is only\Ngoing to get a whole lot worse from here.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:43.60,0:17:46.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Because if the priest has\Nbeen waiting for the new moon?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:46.08,0:17:48.92,Default,,0,0,0,,And the moon is what affects\Nthe Earth's gravitational force?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:49.00,0:17:53.38,Default,,0,0,0,,You've still got to make it through\N36 more hours of this. Listen, Jolene.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:53.66,0:17:56.34,Default,,0,0,0,,The priest got pretty messed up\Nduring his fight with weather.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:56.42,0:17:57.36,Default,,0,0,0,,I saw it myself.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:57.68,0:17:59.39,Default,,0,0,0,,He's got some serious wounds.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:59.56,0:18:03.40,Default,,0,0,0,,This is our chance to kill the\Nbastard while we've got him cornered.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:03.48,0:18:08.25,Default,,0,0,0,,If we just keep climbing up this guardrail,\Nwe can make it to the visitor center.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:08.60,0:18:10.95,Default,,0,0,0,,The priest is headed that way, isn't he?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:11.76,0:18:13.44,Default,,0,0,0,,He is. Up north.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:14.56,0:18:16.56,Default,,0,0,0,,You'll do it, Jolene.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:22.00,0:18:24.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah of course i've\Nalready made up my mind.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:27.54,0:18:31.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes that's it it's those eyes jolene that
Dialogue: 0,0:18:31.10,0:18:32.84,Default,,0,0,0,,expression when you\Nlook into the distance?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:32.92,0:18:39.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Whenever i see you like this my heart is\Nset ablaze emporia let's go yeah sure!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:45.48,0:18:47.26,Default,,0,0,0,,I can read your heart clearly.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:47.66,0:18:50.70,Default,,0,0,0,,You're filled with an intense\Ndetermination to kill the priest.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:50.78,0:18:54.58,Default,,0,0,0,,And yet, it seems that you still yearn\Nfor your father to come save you.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:54.66,0:18:57.22,Default,,0,0,0,,But what you don't see\Nis that I can protect
Dialogue: 0,0:18:57.30,0:19:00.01,Default,,0,0,0,,you better than whether\NOrr Jotaro ever could.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:00.14,0:19:00.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Sooner or later,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:01.05,0:19:03.73,Default,,0,0,0,,you're going to realize\Nthat you want me to be the
Dialogue: 0,0:19:03.82,0:19:06.70,Default,,0,0,0,,one holding you in my arms\Nwhen this is all over.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:08.60,0:19:11.48,Default,,0,0,0,,At the beginning of everything there was
Dialogue: 0,0:19:11.56,0:19:15.92,Default,,0,0,0,,gravity even this round earth of ours was
Dialogue: 0,0:19:16.00,0:19:22.46,Default,,0,0,0,,brought into reality with gravity and with
Dialogue: 0,0:19:22.54,0:19:24.70,Default,,0,0,0,,its gravitational pull\Nthe earth continues to
Dialogue: 0,0:19:24.78,0:19:29.28,Default,,0,0,0,,revolve around the sun the question that\Nstill remains is where on earth am i headed
Dialogue: 0,0:19:29.36,0:19:32.76,Default,,0,0,0,,now what is going to happen next Within my
Dialogue: 0,0:19:32.84,0:19:35.42,Default,,0,0,0,,body and spirit lies the\Nexistence of gravity,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:35.50,0:19:38.32,Default,,0,0,0,,and it shall also exist\Nat the end of the world!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:42.04,0:19:42.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Somebody!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:43.48,0:19:44.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Hello?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:44.46,0:19:46.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Can someone help us?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:46.14,0:19:48.55,Default,,0,0,0,,What the hell is even going on right now?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:48.92,0:19:51.34,Default,,0,0,0,,What is happening to us?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:53.00,0:19:54.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Is someone there?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:54.66,0:19:56.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Anyone help us?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:04.12,0:20:04.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Anybody?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:05.42,0:20:07.26,Default,,0,0,0,,That doesn't look too serious to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:07.34,0:20:08.52,Default,,0,0,0,,We can let it slide.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:08.82,0:20:10.20,Default,,0,0,0,,The phone isn't working.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:10.28,0:20:12.34,Default,,0,0,0,,No signal. Why not?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:13.06,0:20:14.32,Default,,0,0,0,,I have no idea.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:14.82,0:20:18.34,Default,,0,0,0,,I guess it could be that it got\Nbroken in the wreck somehow.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:18.42,0:20:21.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Or maybe it has something to\Ndo with this strange gravity.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:21.46,0:20:22.29,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't know.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:23.30,0:20:26.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Anyways, I wonder what's going\Non everywhere else in the world.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:26.58,0:20:30.23,Default,,0,0,0,,I mean, do you think that a\Nrescue team will possibly show up?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:32.16,0:20:35.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Looks like we made it to\Nthe box offices, Jolene.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:35.90,0:20:37.84,Default,,0,0,0,,And over there is our entrance.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:38.26,0:20:40.85,Default,,0,0,0,,The only way to get\Ninto the visitor center.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:41.46,0:20:44.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Jolene, are you sure the priest\Nis still in this direction?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:48.04,0:20:49.40,Default,,0,0,0,,He's close, yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:49.88,0:20:51.48,Default,,0,0,0,,I can sense him right here.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:55.04,0:20:58.62,Default,,0,0,0,,It almost feels like he was\Njust standing in this spot.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:15.80,0:21:18.12,Default,,0,0,0,,This damn guy, could it be?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:18.40,0:21:20.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Is it really him? But why?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:24.36,0:21:25.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Is it Hail Snake?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:26.18,0:21:28.70,Default,,0,0,0,,No, it looks more like the Green Baby.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:29.30,0:21:30.77,Default,,0,0,0,,This is the priest stand?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:30.98,0:21:32.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Is it in a new form?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:32.50,0:21:34.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, what's going on now?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:44.12,0:21:45.14,Default,,0,0,0,,July, no!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:49.52,0:21:52.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Something fucked up is\Nhappening to my right hand!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:54.56,0:21:59.06,Default,,0,0,0,,I've come to eliminate you for good,\Nsince you couldn't wait two more days.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:26.98,0:22:30.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Although you think I cope.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:31.98,0:22:35.20,Default,,0,0,0,,My head is filled with hope.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:36.98,0:22:43.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Of some place other than here.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:46.98,0:22:50.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Although you think I smile.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:51.76,0:22:55.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Inside and all the while.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:56.98,0:22:59.54,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm wondering.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:59.62,0:23:03.34,Default,,0,0,0,,About my destiny.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:05.92,0:23:09.40,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm thinking about.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:11.78,0:23:14.52,Default,,0,0,0,,All the things.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:16.70,0:23:19.30,Default,,0,0,0,,I'd like to do.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:23.98,0:23:27.24,Default,,0,0,0,,In my life,
Dialogue: 0,0:23:27.32,0:23:31.64,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm a dreamer,
Dialogue: 0,0:23:31.72,0:23:34.40,Default,,0,0,0,,a distant dreamer,
Dialogue: 0,0:23:34.48,0:23:38.16,Default,,0,0,0,,dreaming far
Dialogue: 0,0:23:38.24,0:23:44.44,Default,,0,0,0,,from today.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:50.92,0:23:52.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:19.72,0:24:22.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you.
